[Try a line wrap on occasion, damn ya!  Line breaks added...]

I've managed to get a Debian install started with 16 megabytes of
memory.  You don't actually want to try to USE one of these systems
with only 16 megs of RAM for much work, as you'll run out of memory
very quickly - especially if you want to use X based applications.

For that, I'd recommend at least 64M - Mine's nicely usable as a
workstation with 96M.

These systems take 70ns true-parity SIMMs, in pairs.

