John, this turned out not to be the problem. Your suggestion was as
far as I can see to use the old-disk only driver on primary interface
compared to the new enhanced driver. This did not make any difference.

Except for removing unnecessary RAID support as pointed out by Michal
Jaegermann and the superfluous CONFIG_BLK_DEV_IDEPCI my only change
was

joern:alpha$ diff config-2.2.14.FAIL config-2.2.14.OK 
...
227c220
< CONFIG_ISDN=y
---
> CONFIG_ISDN=m

The problem turned out to be that I included ISDN support with the
Hisax driver for a Teles 8.0/16.0 ISDN card before actually installing
it physically into the box (it is still in my old Pentium box). The
next project will be to see if it is possible to make this work with
the DS10... The start does not that promising. :-)

Thanks to you and Michal for the hints anyway !


