us at least a week and a half. :( A hard disk was segregated from the
hardware RAID 5 array set for this expermentation, but was re-added to the
RAID 5 digital unix array so that we could get a valid BSD label.  After
the RAID 5 rebuilt/overwrote the Linux disk, we could then correctly
obtain all of the BSD disklabeling information required from Digital's
unix filesystem on the hard drive.

