On Mon, 31 Jan 2000 00:23:16 +0900, G. Hugh Song <ghsong@nospam.com> wrote:

>
>The "/dev/printer" socket is missing.  I really do not understand
>what is meant by the word "socket".  A neighborhood's
>Linux system has /dev/printer, while it is missing in my Alpha.
>If anybody knows something about /dev/printer, please
>enlighten me a little bit.

/dev/printer is the "connection" to the printer for printing; if it
is missing, then nothing prints (except for "cat filename > lp0").
>

>BTW, I really do not understand why on earth the printer
>setup is this much difficult every time.  The YaST-based
>configurator in the SuSE-distribution is even worse than
>"printtool" of RedHat.

When YAST configures the printer, it is also doing the configuration
using/for the apsfilter application.

If the "/dev/printer" is not pressent, go to the "spools" and see
if a "lock" file is present; if present, delete them and reboot or
perhaps a reconfigure with YAST would do...



