	Nope.  FreeBSD (and NetBSD) have only a single boot
image.

	The problem is that SRM doesn't know about the IDE
controller, so SRM is unable to boot from it.    The AXPpci33
running SRM really wants the OS on a disk attached to the
built-in SCSI host adapter.

