Depends on the code. In general yes you can (re)compile an application
for Alpha Linux. There are occasions where coders had HUAS (Head Up Ass
Syndrome) and made a bunch of silly assumptions which causes code to not
compile, run incorrectly, etc.

> But how about third party software?  If we need to purchase some nice
> Linux application from some other company, would it also run fine on
> Linux/Alpha.

If the company releases an application for Linux x86 then it will only
run on Linux x86 (an exception would be if it runs under em86.) If they
offer a native Alpha Linux application then there should not be any
problem(s).

> If we'll be purchasing software from some other company (and I'm sure
we
> will at some point), would we be safer to just stick with Linux
running
