According to the SRM-HOWTO you should be able to do a:
>>> boot dka0 -fl "root=/dev/sda3 single"
or something similar. Depends where your root partition
is.

Alternatively you could use abootconf to create a default
configuration for booting in single user mode. Again, this is
described in the SRM-HOWTO. Have a look at alpha-linux.org for the
document.

Rolf



