Paddy Roach wrote:
> 
> Does redhat offer Motif for Linux/Alpha? If so how come there's no mention
> of it on their web site? If not, who does offer it?

Motif is, unfortunately, not free software.  It's a release of the Open
Software Foundation which, despite its name, is not about open source
software.  Motif is a commercial product and must be licensed for a fee
from the OSF.  It would be illegal for Motif to be included in any Linux
distribution without a license, but the cost of the license would
greatly increase the cost of the distro.

There are a number of other window managers available for XFree86 that
look very much like Motif and are included with a number of
distrubutions.

-- Chris Csernica



