Alexander Frink (see_sig_for_faster_reply@BibServer.Physik.Uni-Mainz.DE) wrote:
: In article <HPnACDAO15f4EwRm@afc.support.demon.net>,
: 	Alex Collins <afc@demon.net> writes:
: > and how did you get redhat 6 to work on a Multia. - Which NIC driver did
: > you use?

: The NIC is not a Tulip, but a DE4X5.

The NIC _is_ an older version of Tulip, without fancier transmitters
of the later series, which happens to work pretty nicely with de4x5
_driver_. Names like DE425, DE434, DE435, DE450, DE500 were used
by DEC as their model designations for various Tulip based NICs.

Keep in mind that there are various versions of Tulip cards which will
not work with de4x5 driver at all while for other, not necessarily from
DEC DE... series but generally older, this may be a driver of choice.

  Michal




