This is an example of the srm command you need to use

boot  device-name  -fi 2/vmlinux.gz  -fl "root=/dev/sda2  single"

do a show device at the SRM console ">>>"
and look for the first SCSI device,  dka0 or somthing similar

guess where the kernel is or do a  "show boot*"  *=wildcard
He may have defined the boot device,  boot file and boot flags

If they were defined substitiute those values for the one I use in the
example, but keep the word "single" at the end of the flags  (-fl) and keep
the " around the -fl values..

That will put you in single user mode, you can then reset the passwords or
create a new account for yourself..

JJ


