A few points,

True64 and VMS support was removed from the console (disabled) so the box
could be sold as NT only. And would not carry some of the OS support cost on
the hardware platform. (TRUE64 won't boot, VMS is hobbled) Flash size or
arch. has nothing to do with it.  In some old Alpha's that was the case, but
they stopped shipping years ago (Alpha XL +early AlphaStations), when flash
was expensive and in short supply..


Except for the additional hardware supported by the AlphaBios console
(adaptec and Graphics video ) The 3305 is exactly the same as the 800, in
fact if you invoke Alphabios on the 800, you cannot tell them apart, except
for the color of their case, NT onlys were white and called white boxes :^)


No you cannot load the 800 srm, they though of that :^)

Use the latest tulip.c , works really well. I've has good luck with the
2.2.14 kernel


JJ


