A couple of pointers:

The reason you can't load TRU64 or VMS is because of the flash that carries
the PAL - it's too small to support these 2 OS's. The 3305 was a cheaper
version of the 800 series machine, and meant for NT only. :(

 I've found that re-compiling the kernel seems to remove a lot of flakiness
from the machine under RH6.0. During the kernel re-compile, you can select
the specific DE500 driver, but don't. I've had better luck with the Tulip
driver. I think I remember a patch for Alpha linux that deals with this on
the RedHat site, too. BTW, the DE500-BA uses the newer 21143 Tulip chipset -
which is now owned and produced by Intel. You can get specs for the chip
there.

Ron

