Actually I do it a little differently and this seems to work
nicely on my SX164.

I have a small vfat (MSDOS) partition, which is needed by the
Alphabios on the SX164.  I put milo and linload.exe in there.
THis is after you have the operating system installed and can
boot linux using the milo floppy.  Say this small (2 MB will do)
is hda5 or hda6.

dd if=/dev/fd0 of=/dev/hdaX  where X is the partition number of
your DOS partition will copy the floppy image over.  You can
then edit your alphabios boot parameters to choose this partition
and linload.exe for the second line and some phony partition and
milo in the third line.

Your fourth line would then be

boot hda1:/boot/vmlinuz root=/dev/hda1

if hda1 contains the /boot directory.  Otherwise, change
the number to the partition where this directory is located.

Bob



