That's technically just an Alpha Server 3305. It says 3000 on it, but 
that's not the model number you would go by to get any information from 
Compaq. I have a 3300 myself that I'm getting ready to install Debian on.

: 
: Is there a MILO created for this version? Can this server support Linux
: (or Tru64?)

As far as I know there is no MILO for it, and it won't run Tru64, but it 
_will_ run Linux if you install it from the SRM console. Appended below 
is part of a message by John Jemiolo from the AXP mailing list that I 
found informative:

---
This is a similar box to the AlphaServer 800, You can load and run Linux 
from SRM on the 3300. On power-up switch to SRM by typing F2 to get into 
setup then follow the menus to advanced cmos setup (setup->cmos 
setup->advanced (F6))-> 3/4 down the page is the console selection, 
select 
SRM Unix Then save and power cycle. 

Although you can select the correct console, these boxes will NOT run 
TRU64 
Unix or VMS, but Linux will run just fine, and you get the latest pal 
code.. 

To get back to AlphaBios from SRM type "set os_type NT" at the srm prompt 
">>>" and power cycle. 

To install follow the guide at 

http://www.digital.com/alphaserver/linux/install_guide.html 

The quide is for xp1000, ds10 and ds20, "but" SRM Installs are all the 
SAME. just use the generic single cpu kernel. 

a note though make sure the graphics card in the box is supported by 
Linux/Alpha. 
---

I haven't yet followed these steps because I'm waiting for the drive 
carrier for my SCA drive (didn't know my server didn't come with any), 
but I'd be interested in sharing experience with anyone else who has a 
server from this series.

-->ben fulton




