> > AFAIK, you just treat it like a unix host.  In Redhat's printtool you'd
> > choose "Remote unix (lpd) queue."
> 
> Fine OK I Use the ip as host name, but what do i use as queue name?

I have a few Jet Directs, both internals and an external with 3 ports.

I address them as raw, like so:

This one is external and on the 2d port
oki393:\
        :sd=/var/spool/lpd/oki393:\
        :mx#0:\
        :sh:\
        :rm=hp500x1:\
        :rp=raw2:

This is an internal installed in an HP 4M
hp_svc:\
        :sd=/var/spool/lpd/hp_svc:\
        :mx#0:\
        :sh:\
        :rm=hp4m:\
        :rp=raw:\
        :if=/var/spool/lpd/hp_svc/filter:



