>I can "ls hda1:" and see the files but I don't see a "vmlinux.gz" should
>there be one????

You're *nearly* there.

You need to determine which file is the actual kernel file.

It is apparently *not* /vmlinux.gz

MILO> ls hda1:

will list you the files in the root directory; watch for the file
vmlinuz, which I'd speculate to be the most likely candidate.

If so, then the command is:
boot hda1:vmlinuz root=/dev/hda1

If there's nothing that looks like a kernel in the root directory, you
might check in /boot, thus:
MILO> ls hda1:boot

which hopefully will provide you with a suitable kernel.
