I'm not sure about the Multia, but this works on several other SRM
systems I've used.

There is a variable that controls what happens when you get to SRM.
It's called auto_action, or something close to that.

  Get to >>>
  Do a "show a*" to see what it's called.
  Try "set auto_action foo" to get a list of the legal values
  You want to set it to "BOOT"

