Hi,

Ruffian, along with the 2.2.9 kernel (vsn. 1.09 of the Real Time Clock
Driver drivers/char/rtc.c) has a millennium bug. Some adventurous code to
determine the type of clock from the year number stored within breaks on
Ruffian with year 2000. In fact, I'm sure that Ruffian clock is not
supported at all and only worked by accident between 1996 and 1999 ;-)

Okay, it's easy to fix for Ruffian, but then it will probably break on the
other machines! I think this really should go into some run-time
configuration option or a proper detection of the board type in use.
Unfortunately the seems to be a problem with the e-mail adress of the rtc
author :-(
 
So, in the mean time, any Ruffian user should check if he doesn't life
already in 2052. Also, I can tell them my cheap and dirty patch, but this
is not for public, really ;-)
 
