I think I've determined the problem. . . there appears to be a conflict on
the PCI bus between the ncr53c810 controller and the FA310TX NIC.   After
verifying that all my SCSI devices (CD-ROM and disk) were configured
properly, I noticed that the only time the SCSI timeouts were occuring was
when I would write something to the disk across the network (via SMB or
other such service).  Once I switched the cards and set the external NIC
(the de4x5 compatible card on the multia motherboard) to be the interal
interface and the FA310TX (tulip driver) to be the external interface, the
problems stopped.   I have not yet had a chance to swap out the FA310TX with
another NIC.  Until I do that, I will not know whether it is the card or the
actual PCI slot that is the problem.  If it is indeed the slot, I'll try
using a PCMCIA NIC instead, as that's the only available PCI slot in the
box.

I have seen several posts on this ng about multias being finicky machines. .
. I can vouch for this!


