Hello all -

I had trouble gettting a Yamaha 6416S CD-RW working on my PC164 with 
cdrecord.

I found the solution was pretty simple:  I finally took a look at the 
/etc/cdrecord.conf file.  The device variable was set to "dev=yamaha".  
I changed this to "dev=/dev/sg0" and everything seems to work now.
What tipped me off were the error messages returned by "cdrecord 
-checkdrive".

Well I feel silly now...

I did take the recommendations in the provided docs and increased the 
SHMMAX variable to 0x1000000 in the include/asm-alpha/shmparm.h of the 
kernel tree.  Don't know the overall effect on my machine yet though.

ed

-- 
