First read the MILO-Howto (included on the CD I hope).
It tell you howto get Linux running on the machine. BTW there is more
stuff on the CD that you can read to install the machine (/README and
maybe more).

-Setup ARC to boot MILO (I think you can boot milo right from the cd
within arc (never tried it), else make a milo floppie with the
diskimages contained in /milo/images on cd).
-From MILO boot the linux kernel with the CD as root filesystem

From there the install will be very like installing an i386 machine.
But remember to make a small (few MB are enough) dos partition so you
can boot milo directly form ARC without cds or floppies.

